proportional to transcription, and no API key or remote service use is requested by the skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill metadata offers a Homebrew install of the openai-whisper formula and requires the whisper binary; this is purpose-aligned but depends on the user's package manager trust in that formula.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are narrow, user-directed command examples with no prompt overrides, hidden agent instructions, unrelated data access, or automatic execution.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses that Whisper models download to ~/.cache/whisper on first run; this cache persistence is expected for local model use and does not indicate a background service or privilege escalation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is local speech-to-text using the Whisper CLI, and the runtime examples are limited to transcribing or translating user-provided audio files.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you are comfortable using Homebrew to install the Whisper CLI and allowing model files to be cached locally. Review audio file paths before running commands, since transcription output is written where you direct it.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013563751}}}}}